    - target: {fileID: 4459353801605931126, guid: c0a0edafc9d430b43b3b6107976bbe1c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'Now I remember you.



        The third machine roared to life. Mana
        surged through the pipes, and the last flower shone so brightly that I had
        to close my eyes.



        And then, I remembered everything.



        The
        garden. The promise. The person I loved more than my own life.



        When
        magic began to disappear, I tried to save them by taking all the flower''s
        power. But the spell was stronger than I was. The flower survived, the world
        lost its magic, and my memories became the price of my survival.



        I
        didn''t build these machines to become powerful.



        I built them
        because I couldn''t bear to live without remembering the one person who mattered
        most.



        Now I remember your name. Your voice. The promise I made.



        The
        flower is almost gone. I could take the remaining mana and learn the very
        last piece of the truth. Or I could stop the machines and let the last source
        of magic live.



        I reached for the lever.



        For the first
        time in all these years, I knew what I had to do.



        Some memories
        return not so we can repeat the past, but so we can finally let it go.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4459353801605931126, guid: c0a0edafc9d430b43b3b6107976bbe1c, type: 3}
