    - target: {fileID: 4223408136155989217, guid: c0a0edafc9d430b43b3b6107976bbe1c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_AnchoredPosition.y
      value: -2.8829956
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4459353801605931126, guid: c0a0edafc9d430b43b3b6107976bbe1c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'I remember this light...



        I stood in the middle of a dead
        garden. Once, thousands of magical flowers bloomed here, each shining like
        a tiny star. Now, only one remained.



        I couldn''t remember how
        I had come here. I couldn''t remember my name, my home, or even my own face.
        But when I touched its petals, a voice echoed inside my head.



        "Please...
        don''t let it fade."



        I didn''t know who had spoken. Somehow, it
        made me want to cry.



        So I built the first Mana Machine. If the
        flower could return even a fragment of what I had lost, I would draw every
        last drop of mana from it.



        Even if it became my final mistake.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
